# `tsc -b`'s own incremental-build cache. Left uncopied for the same reason `dist` is: a stale
# `*.tsbuildinfo` from the host (this repo's own `.gitignore` already keeps it untracked, but
# .dockerignore is a separate allowlist) makes `tsc -b` trust old build-completeness bookkeeping
# and skip emitting `dist/` entirely even though none exists in the build context -- caught by
# actually running this exact `pnpm install && pnpm -r build` sequence against a copy of the real
# build context during this phase's verification: every package's `dist/` came up missing.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Node-only image (Phase 11a; Python source tree removed in the cutover phase that followed):
# everything below is docs/fixtures/dev tooling the running apps/server never reads at build- or
# run-time. Excluded from the build context entirely. Every pnpm-workspace member (packages/*,
# apps/*, tools/*) is deliberately left out of this list: the lockfile is workspace-aware, so
# pruning an actual workspace package out of the build context would break
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. Packages not needed at runtime (tools/*) are instead removed
# from the build stage's own filesystem *after* `pnpm -r build`, in the Dockerfile itself -- see
# its comments.
/examples
/vendor
/docs
/scripts
/.github
